/-!
# The determinant model of the Weil pairing: construction, classification, existence

The catalog file `Cryptography.WeilPairingBLS` *axiomatises* a Weil pairing on the
`n`-torsion of a Weierstrass curve (bilinear, alternating, `n`-torsion valued,
nondegenerate).  This file removes the axiom in the only place where it can be removed
by pure algebra, and classifies all possible pairings.

Main results.

* `AltPairing` : the bare alternating bi-additive interface, extracted from a
  `WeilPairing` by `WeilPairing.toAltPairing`.
* `AltPairing.pair_zsmul_left/right`, `AltPairing.skew` : full `ℤ`-bilinearity and
  skew-symmetry from alternation alone.
* `AltPairing.pair_coords` : **classification.** On a group generated by two elements
  `e₁, e₂`, every alternating pairing is the `ζ`-th power of the determinant form,
  `e(a e₁ + b e₂, c e₁ + d e₂) = ζ ^ (ad - bc)` with `ζ = e(e₁,e₂)`.  In particular two
  alternating pairings that agree on a basis agree everywhere
  (`AltPairing.ext_of_basis`).
* `detPairing` : the explicit determinant pairing on `(ZMod n)²` with values in
  `Multiplicative (ZMod n)`, proved alternating, `n`-torsion and **nondegenerate**.
* `weilPairingOfEquiv` : **existence.** Any Weierstrass curve whose `n`-torsion is
  isomorphic to `(ZMod n)²` carries a Weil pairing in the sense of the catalog
  structure.  Together with `detPairing_nondegenerate` this shows that the axioms of
  `WeilPairing` are consistent and non-vacuous.
* `AltPairing.orderOf_root_of_nondegenerate` : conversely, a nondegenerate alternating
  pairing on `(ZMod n)²` forces its root of unity `ζ` to have exact order `n`.
-/

